e that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-12T22:23:23.402919-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 490793, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/without/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial9.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 33291, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "free_disk_gb": 36.18, "fresh_subagents": 0, "functional_pass": null, "gate_cell": false, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170344 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/<REDACTED_HEX>/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "<HOST>", "image_digest": null, "image_scan_copies": [], "installed_anthropic": "2.0.50", "instance_id": "8187537343833955709", "instruction_app_rewrite": true, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "load_proof": "pass", "load_proof_basis": "user_agent", "load_proof_reason": "User-Agent 2.0.50", "loaded_anthropic": "2.0.50", "lock_wait_s": 0.0, "lockfile": "bun.lock", "lockfile_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "machine": "<HOST>", "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_match_reason": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "network_mode": "local", "off_protocol": false, "opencode_cache": "/h1/opencode-src", "output_tail": "rd is turned into one 64-character string (empty squares become `.`). The en passant square is reduced to just its file letter, and the move counters are dropped.\n2. **Generate candidate moves:** there is one rule for each piece, starting square and destination (sliding moves also require the squares in between to be empty). If the rule matches the original position, it adds a new line with that move made. This covers pawn pushes (including the double push, which sets the en passant square), captures, promotion to queen only, en passant, and castling.\n3. **Remove illegal moves:** the original line is deleted. Then one rule per king square deletes every candidate where the white king is attacked by a knight, pawn, king, or a sliding piece with a clear path.\n   - Castling uses temporary marker letters, so the king's start square and the square it passes through are checked as well as where it lands. The markers become an empty square and a rook afterwards.\n4. **Update castling rights:** each right is dropped if the king or that rook is no longer on its home square, which covers moves and captures alike. An empty field becomes `-`.\n5. **Repack:** the board goes back to normal FEN with ` b`, and ` 0 0` is added as the move counters.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- After any double pawn push, the output always shows the en passant square, even when Black can't actually capture. `check.py` accepts this because it also compares with that field replaced by `-`.\n- When run exactly as in the brief (plain `re.sub` each time), it takes about 2 seconds per position. Nearly all of that is recompiling the regexes, because Python's regex cache only holds 512 patterns. Precompiled, it takes about 0.2 seconds.\n- If White has no legal moves (checkmate or stalemate), the function returns `['']` rather than an empty list. That's unavoidable with this setup, because splitting any string always gives at least one item.\n\nThe generator script is at `/tmp/work/gen.py` if you want to rebuild the file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "pin_source": "override", "pin_source_class": "override", "probe_method": "embedded", "protocol_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "provider_loaded_mismatch": null, "provider_loaded_source": "embedded", "provider_loaded_version": "2.0.50", "provider_pin_sha256": "<REDACTED_HEX>", "provider_trace": "off", "provider_version_proven": true, "provider_version_source": "embedded", "provider_versions": {"@ai-sdk/anthropic": "2.0.50"}, "proxy_cost_usd": 1.1167784, "proxy_observed": [{"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tokens": null, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": "none"}, {"reasoning_tok